From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: tve: don't read an uninitialised preferred mode

tve_parse_dt() and tve_parse_dt_legacy() both declare "int ret, val" and
then read "rockchip,tvemode" into val. of_property_read_u32() leaves val
untouched when the property is absent, and the absent branch assigns
tve->preferred_mode twice:

	if (ret < 0) {
		tve->preferred_mode = 0;	/* immediately overwritten */
	} else if (val > 1) {
		...
	}
	tve->preferred_mode = val;		/* val is indeterminate */

So a tree that leaves the property out gets a stack-garbage preferred
mode instead of the intended 0. rockchip_tve_get_modes() then compares it
against the cvbs_mode[] index to set DRM_MODE_TYPE_PREFERRED; any value
other than 0 or 1 marks neither 720x576i nor 720x480i as preferred, and
userspace picks whichever mode it happens to enumerate first. The two
vendor RK3528 TV-box trees in the wild both omit the property.

Assign val in the absent branch so the single store below sees the
intended default.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
index f34b6d8..f7501b1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
@@ -711,7 +711,7 @@ static int tve_parse_dt(struct device_node *np, struct rockchip_tve *tve)
 
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(np, "rockchip,tvemode", &val);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		tve->preferred_mode = 0;
+		val = 0;
 	} else if (val > 1) {
 		dev_err(tve->dev, "tve mode value invalid\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -802,7 +802,7 @@ static int tve_parse_dt_legacy(struct device_node *np, struct rockchip_tve *tve)
 
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(np, "rockchip,tvemode", &val);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		tve->preferred_mode = 0;
+		val = 0;
 	} else if (val > 1) {
 		dev_err(tve->dev, "tve mode value invalid\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
